This file contains a list of the known bugs in the dltools package.

* dlplay: when playing out transport streams with MPEG-1 audio the audio
doesn't loop like the video does, becoming corrupt on the second pass

* dlplay: the -a, --firstframe option is parsed and range checked but its value
is never used, so the option silently has no effect and playback always starts
at the first frame in the input

* dlplay: a transport stream from a socket has one read position shared by every
format filter, so the video and audio filters discard each other's packets and both
streams lose data; only file sources give each filter an independent reader
